  "body": "Products\nNew Collection\nAll Products\nFurniture\nLighting\nObjects\nOutdoor\nCollections\nClassics\nEU Ecolabel\nConfigurators\nDesigners\nInspiration\nStories\nCases\nOur Community\nPublications\nCatalogues\nVisit\nLille Petra Café\nPetra Hotel\nShowrooms\nImpact\nProfessionals\nCases\nCatalogues\nUpholstery Collection\nConfigurators\nShowrooms\nDownloads\nStore Locator\n \nSearch\nFlowerpot VP9\nVerner Panton\n1968\nVariants\nZesty Orange\nStock item\nFlowerpot Collection\nFlowerpotVP1\nFlowerpotVP1\nFlowerpotVP2\nFlowerpotVP3\nFlowerpotVP4\nFlowerpotVP7\nFlowerpotVP8\nFlowerpotVP9\nFlowerpotVP10\nFlowerpotVP12\nFlowerpot ChandelierVP1\nFlowerpot ChandelierVP10\nFind Dealer\nExplore The Flowerpot Collection\nprev\nnext\nslide 1 of 4\n1234\nDescription\nReflecting the same iconic design as the Flowerpot table lamp, the petite proportions of the VP9 lamp have the added advantage of being mobile. The deliberately lightweight design and cordless feature allow the lamp to be easily moved from table to counter as needed.\nProduct Details\nDownloads\nSpecifications\nImpact\nMaterials\nManufacturer \nMaintenance & Care\nMomento Jug JH38 | Flowerpot VP9 | Collect SC80 | Collect SC79\nFlowerpot VP9\nDESIGNED BY\nVerner Panton\n\nVerner Panton (1926 – 1998) is known worldwide for his avant-garde work and prolific experimentation with materials, shapes, and most importantly – colour. Throughout his career, he would advocate that colour had both a central meaning and function in design and that it should be used as a tool to enhance everyday life.\n\nLearn More\nRelated Products\nFlowerpot Chandelier VP10\nCanopy\nVerner Panton\n2 Variants\nTopan VP13\nTable lamp\nVerner Panton\n3 Variants\nNumbra TY3\nPortable Lamp\nTeruhiro Yanagihara\nNumbra TY1\nPendant\nTeruhiro Yanagihara\n\nFounded in 2010 in Copenhagen, &Tradition is an international brand built on a Danish legacy of craftsmanship and design. Whether our starting point is new or reissued, we are passionate about designing the classics of tomorrow. Telling stories with originality, we believe in empowering our employees and network of creatives, designers and partners to take an active part in our journey as a brand. With the wellbeing of people and respect for the planet at the forefront, we strive to always act conscientiously.\n\nCOMPANY\nAbout Us\nImpact\nCareers\nPress\nShowrooms\nStore Locator\nINSPIRATION\nNewsletter\nCatalogues\nStories\nCases\nDesigners\nDIGITAL RESOURCES\nDownloads\nProfessionals\nPCON\nMaintenance & Care\nUpholstery Collection\nAssembly Videos\nLight Source Recommendations\nSUPPORT\nContact Us\nPrivacy Policy\nCookie Settings\nFood Administration Report\nGeneral Terms & Conditions\nInstagramLinkedInFacebookPinterest\nCopyright © &Tradition\n\nSign up to our newsletter",
